meta {
  name: Sign contract (e-signature callback)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/esign
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "eventId": "set by the pre-request script",
    "type": "envelope.completed",
    "envelopeId": "{{envelopeId}}",
    "documentHash": "{{documentHash}}",
    "occurredAt": "set by the pre-request script"
  }
}

script:pre-request {
  // Plays the e-signature provider: signs the raw body with ESIGN_WEBHOOK_SECRET.
  // Needs Bruno's Developer Mode (JavaScript sandbox) for require("crypto").
  const crypto = require("crypto");
  const body = JSON.stringify({
    eventId: crypto.randomUUID(),
    type: "envelope.completed",
    envelopeId: bru.getEnvVar("envelopeId"),
    documentHash: bru.getEnvVar("documentHash"),
    occurredAt: new Date().toISOString(),
  });
  const timestamp = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);
  const signature = crypto
    .createHmac("sha256", bru.getEnvVar("esignSecret"))
    .update(`${timestamp}.${body}`)
    .digest("hex");
  req.setHeader("Content-Type", "application/json");
  req.setHeader("X-Esign-Signature", `t=${timestamp},v1=${signature}`);
  req.setBody(body);
}

docs {
  The provider's callback, normally sent by the simulated e-signature service when the student signs. It is authenticated by `X-Esign-Signature: t=<unix seconds>,v1=<hex HMAC-SHA256 of "<t>.<raw body>">` with `ESIGN_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (`esignSecret` in the environment, the compose default).

  Answers 200 with the contract's status. A callback about an envelope settled by an earlier one (completed after a decline, expired after signing) also answers 200, with the status as it is, and changes nothing; 409 `envelope_not_recorded` is for an envelope not saved yet, which a retry can fix.

  The script needs Developer Mode (sandbox selector next to the environment). If it answers 401 `invalid_webhook_signature`, sign from a terminal instead: `pnpm esign:sign {{contractId}}` (add `--decline` to decline).
}
